It's fun having pets in Nethack, but there's a bunch of stuff that you 
should be able to do with them, things that are logical and not too 
excessive, at least in my humble opinion.  Here's my ideas:

Give command:  allows you to give items to a humanoid pet.  The pet will 
automatically wield any weapon you give it, wear any armor you give it, and 
don any amulet/ring/etc you give it, subject to the usual rules, ie lawful 
pets won't wield chaotic weapons, pets will refuse to hold/use cursed items, 
etc.  The pet will carry stuff up to just before the point of being 
burdened, any items given to it after that point will be exchanged randomly 
with items already held and the old item will be dropped to the floor.  You 
may give items to a non-humanoid pet just as you would to a humanoid one if 
you have first applied a "saddlebag" or similar item to it.  The "saddlebag" 
allows the non-humanoid pet to hold items just like a humanoid pet, ie to 
just before burdening.  Amorphous and non-solid pets may not have a 
saddlebag applied to them, obviously.

Take command:  allows you to access a pet's inventory and take items from it 
into your inventory, just as if the pet were a chest or similar storage 
device.

Exception:  All non-amorphous, solid pets may be given an amulet, since it 
counts as a collar for the non-humanoid ones.  So you can give your pet your 
choice of an amulet of unchanging (protects against those pesky polytraps), 
for those most precious of already poly-resistant pets an amulet of life 
saving, or any other amulet you choose...including the: Magic Collar.

Magic Collar:  New type of amulet, may only be worn by a pet.  Does several 
things. While wearing a Magic Collar:

1.  a pet never becomes untame
2.  a regular whistle acts as a magic whistle, for the the magic collar 
wearing pet
3.  a magic whistle will level teleport a magic collar wearing pet to you


I'm sure all of these need work, but they would be a start to making pets a 
more fun part of Nethack.  Thoughts?

